en_US:
Welcome! I'm Hawes, the
assistant director.{VAR BE01}
Since you were kind enough to visit,
I'll give you a tour of the museum.{VAR BE01}

This skeleton is of a Dragon-type
Pokémon.{VAR BE01}
There's a theory that it had an accident
while it was flying around the world, and{VAR BE00}
so it became a Fossil.{VAR BE01}

This rock is amazing! It's a meteorite!{VAR BE01}
It contains some kind of energy
from space.{VAR BE01}

Oh, this? It's an ordinary old stone.{VAR BE01}
It was found near the desert, but other
than the fact that it's old, it doesn't{VAR BE00}
seem to have any value...{VAR BE01}
We only display it because it's rather
pretty to look at.{VAR BE01}

At the end of the Gym, a very strong
and kind Gym Leader is waiting.{VAR BE01}
By the way, the Gym Leader Lenora
happens to be my wife!{VAR BE01}

Team Plasma: So you've come, Gym Leader.{VAR BE01}
We, Team Plasma, claim this museum's
Dragon Skull in the name of{VAR BE00}
Pokémon liberation!{VAR BE01}

Cheren: So I can't battle the Gym Leader
because of Team Plasma, huh...{VAR BE01}
What a bother.

Skeletal specimens are so mysterious...{VAR BE01}
From the outside, you can't see their
functional, efficient design.{VAR BE01}
It's almost as if it is an embodiment of
their former essence... So fascinating!

Those thugs sure were bold...{VAR BE01}
It's almost as if they believe they are
doing the right thing.
